  "term": "Zyprexa",
  "definition": "Zyprexa is a brand name for olanzapine, a synthetic antipsychotic drug. It acts on several brain receptor systems, especially serotonin and dopamine receptors, and is also noted in the source as having antinausea and antiemetic effects.",
